---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Show a workspace and the parts asked for; the parts are fetched at the same time.
Without --with it prints the name, id and member count.

USAGE
  holst workspace show [<ws>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  ws   The workspace: id or part of its name; your only workspace if left out

FLAGS
  --with parts   Also show these parts, comma separated: members, activity, plan, plans, sso, domains, created; none by default
  --user user    Only this member in members, activity and created: a user id; everyone by default

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst ws show
  $ holst ws show easy --with members,activity
  $ holst ws show easy --with created --user 1a2b3c4d

LEARN MORE
  How a workspace is given: `holst ws -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
